changes={
('.data','inferred_type'):'Existing source and split objects have a136-byte initialized section: assertion filename/expression text followed by two consecutive HSD_Chan descriptors. chan0 is GX_COLOR0 with transparent-black ambient and transparent-white material; chan1 is GX_ALPHA0 with opaque-black colors. Both disable lighting, use register sources, no lights, clamp diffuse and no attenuation. Source does not mutate these presets.',
('.sdata2','data_flow'):'Pool literals support RGB filter coefficients, blur spacing and camera setup/aspect correction. Existing objects store1/64=0.015625 for source division by64, plus2.0 for the second offset; they do not store64.0. A2^52 conversion double also occurs. Geometry/camera results flow to GX and HSD calls.',
('lb_80011AC4','purpose'):'Loads runtime light chains from a NULL-terminated LightList table and attaches each entry first animation chain. Between entries it overwrites the previous returned head next pointer with the new head; this is not a tail append of arbitrary multi-light sublists.',
('lb_80011AC4','data_flow'):'Each desc is loaded into a runtime chain and anims[0], when present, is attached. The previous loaded head is passed to HSD_LObjSetNext, which directly replaces its next pointer. Earlier descriptor-chain tails can therefore be disconnected when another table entry is linked. first records the first loaded result and is returned; an initially empty table leaves first uninitialized.',
('lb_80011AC4','state_behavior'):'Walks until a NULL table entry. Each noninitial loaded head replaces prev->next, rather than being appended after the previous chain tail. First is assigned only during an iteration; an empty table has undefined return. Only anims[0] is attached, with no requested starting frame or animation evaluation.',
('lb_80011AC4','inferred_type'):'HSD_LObj* lb_80011AC4(LightList** list), accepting a NULL-terminated pointer table. Each descriptor may load a chain, but linking uses each loaded head, so preserving every light requires compatible single-head resource organization. Empty input has no defined return value.',
('lb_80011E24','state_behavior'):'NULL root/output returns0. Requests terminate at-1; every other signed value consumes an output slot. Traversal descends unless INSTANCE, then follows siblings or ascends via parents. It stops at a NULL parent, not explicitly at the supplied root: an interior root can escape its subtree. Decreasing target relative to retained traversal position restarts at root; otherwise resumes. Negative targets other than-1 exhaust without matching; missing sentinel is not checked.',
('lb_8001204C','state_behavior'):'NULL root/output/indices returns0, and nonpositive count executes no request loop. For positive count every index produces a pointer orNULL. INSTANCE children are skipped. Parent ascent is not bounded to the supplied root, so an interior root may traverse outside its subtree. A target below retained traversal position restarts at root; otherwise it resumes.',
('lb_800122F0','inferred_name'):'lbSpDisplay_SetupTintedImageTexture',
('lb_800122F0','data_flow'):'Initializes and loads the caller texture from image fields. Exactly zero factor routes texture RGB through one stage; nonzero factor computes three RGB coefficient vectors and uses swap tables1-3 over three accumulating stages. The nominal factor1 matrix is approximately luminance times(1,0.9,0.8), assuming the expected swap-table definitions and target byte-conversion behavior. Factor is not clamped; alpha setup for stage0 remains the caller responsibility, while stages1/2 preserve prior alpha.',
('lb_800138D8','inferred_type'):'void lb_800138D8(HSD_GObj* gobj, s8 size). Assigns size to CameraBlurData.blur_size, a u8; negative signed values wrap into128-255. It sets mode1 but neither validates user data nor initializes tint_factor.',
('lb_800138EC','data_flow'):'GObj_Create(14,15,0) supplies classifier14, process-link15 and link priority0. Allocates an orthographic640x480 camera with eye(0,0,1), interest0, near0, far2. Allocates CameraBlurData and writes position, scale, alpha, mode0, image and NULL callback; blur_size and tint_factor are not initialized. Installs the free callback and chosen renderer at caller render priority. The C body has no return statement.',
('lb_800138EC','inferred_type'):'Declared HSD_GObj* lb_800138EC(HSD_ImageDesc* img, GObj_RenderFunc render_func, int prio, s8 alpha, float pos_x, float pos_y, float scale_x, float scale_y). Current callers consume a returned GObj, but the pinned C body reaches its end without a return statement; source alone does not establish a valid returned object. This is a decompilation/source limitation, not a guaranteed constructor return.',
('lb_800138EC','state_behavior'):'Sets mode0 and callbackNULL, plus supplied placement, scale, image and alpha. It leaves blur_size/tint_factor unwritten and has no local allocation-failure cleanup. Switching to mode1 sets blur_size but still requires tint_factor initialization by a caller/event. A custom renderer replaces default composition. User-data removal frees only the user-state allocation through the registered callback.',
('lb_80013B14','game_mapping'):'Adjusts one exact legacy perspective aspect value and caps scissor right/bottom at640/480 for scene presentation. It does not constrain left/top, viewport or lower bounds and therefore does not guarantee a valid rectangle wholly inside the screen.',
('fn_80013614','state_behavior'):'Calls the event using the user-data pointer captured before invocation, then tests that same record. Mode1 draws21 samples and nonzero tint sets scissor(0,110,640,290); other modes draw one quad. There is no local scissor restoration or camera-end call. Event callbacks must preserve the live GObj/user-data assumptions; replacing user_data does not cause this invocation to reread its pointer. Both drawing paths invalidate HSD state mask2 through their respective helpers.'}
additions={('.sdata','purpose'):'Holds assertion filename lobj.h and expression lobj for the inlined HSD_LObjSetNext nonnull check used during light-list linking. Existing split/source sections contain16/13 bytes including padding.',('.sdata','inferred_type'):'Small initialized string pool: NUL-terminated lobj.h at offset0, one padding byte, and NUL-terminated lobj at offset8. Existing objects identify payload; source object size13 and split size16 differ only in trailing padding.',('lb_800121FC','state_behavior'):'Writes metadata before asserting image_ptr isNULL. Width/height narrow to descriptor fields before sizing; dimensions, format and backing capacity are not independently validated. Nonzero preload result is borrowed without allocation; otherwise allocate rounded byte count. No local allocation failure check, buffer clearing or ownership tag is installed.',('lb_80012994','state_behavior'):'Always emits the fixed21-sample sequence, even for blur_size0 or caller alpha0. Only the center sample uses caller alpha; all20 others use constants0x7F..0xF2. Source accesses synthetic GXColor temporaries via negative indices relative to GXTexObj, so the observed target-oriented sequence is not a portable-C memory-safety claim. Ends with HSD_StateInvalidate(2).'}
